course: dictionary
lesson: 9396
title: Sprint: fast and short
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To sprint is to run as fast as you can for a short distance. Context clues show this. «He lay stiff as a plank for an hour, then sprinted to his parents' room so fast he hit the door frame.» The word «so fast» and the door frame tell you sprinted means running very quickly.
explain: A sprint is short. A long-distance run is different, because you pace yourself and save some energy for later. Ask yourself: is the distance short and the speed high? If yes, it is a sprint.
explain: Sprint can also be a noun. «She won the school sprint» means she won a short, very fast race. The word can name a race, or describe a burst of fast action.
fact: To sprint is to run as fast as you can for a short distance.
fact: A sprint is a short, very fast race, like the 100 metres.
fact: «Sprint» can be a verb (I sprint, he sprinted, they are sprinting) or a noun (a sprint, sprints).
fact: A sprint can also mean a short burst of hard work done quickly.
fact: Capybaras can sprint at about 35 km/h, which shows how fast a sprint can be.
exercise: «He sprinted to his parents' room so fast he hit the door frame.» What does sprinted mean? | Walked slowly and carefully | Jumped up and down | Crawled quietly under the bed | *Ran as fast as he could for a short distance
exercise: On sports day, which race is a sprint? | A long run where you pace yourself over many miles | A slow walk around the field | A quiet game of catch | *A 100 metre race run flat out
exercise: Which sentence uses sprint to mean a short burst of hard work done quickly? | The bus took a long route through the hills | Jay lay still for an hour reading a book | The cat slept all afternoon in the sun | *Mum had a sprint on the housework and tidied the whole house in twenty minutes
test: Capybaras can sprint at about 35 km/h. Which word means nearly the same as sprint, meaning run very fast for a short distance? | Yawn | *Dash | Stroll | Doze
test: Yesterday Sam ___ to catch the bus. (sprint) | Sprinting | Sprints | *Sprinted | Sprint
exam: In «She won the school sprint», what kind of word is sprint? | An adjective, because it describes the girl | A pronoun, because it replaces a name | A verb, because it shows an action | *A noun, because it names a race
